{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/105746","id":2481410385,"node_id":"PR_kwDOAO6SJc6T51FR","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/105746","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/105746.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/105746.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/105746","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/105746/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/105746/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/105746/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/statuses/e160040f0c61e422f8ee41880e627daf8b10ccca","number":105746,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"Remove Jolt Physics project setting \"Areas Detect Static Bodies\"","user":{"login":"mihe","id":4884246,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ4ODQyNDY=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4884246?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe","html_url":"https://github.com/mihe","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"As talked about in the recent update of Jolt Physics (#104449) and originally discussed in jrouwe/JoltPhysics#1476, this PR removes the project setting `physics/jolt_physics_3d/simulation/areas_detect_static_bodies`, effectively making it permanently `true`, in favor of leveraging the newly introduced `JPH::PhysicsSystem::SetSimCollideBodyVsBody` functionality, and the `JPH::CollideShapeVsShapePerLeaf` helper function, which lets us configure the amount of contacts that are generated (and thus cached) by Jolt as part of the collision detection that it does during simulation, thus mitigating the performance impact of enabling this project setting.\r\n\r\n> [!WARNING]\r\n> This is technically a breaking change, and potentially quite pervasive, depending on the project, since areas that were maybe not meant to detect static bodies now will. This does however bring Jolt Physics in line with how Godot Physics behaves (although it has its own issues with areas and static bodies) so I feel there's reasonable justification for just removing this setting completely rather than just changing its default to `true` and allowing people to disable it, especially when considering the current experimental label of the Jolt Physics integration.\r\n\r\nThis project setting has become a fairly popular one to enable over the years, largely due to Godot Physics supporting this already, and despite efforts to warn people about its ill effects in Jolt Physics specifically, most seem to just go ahead and enable it anyway, since the alternatives/workarounds can be inconvenient and/or unintuitive.\r\n\r\nAs such, this removes a fairly significant performance footgun, since by default Jolt would otherwise (when enabling this project setting) generate contacts for every overlapping triangle when an `Area3D` overlaps with a `ConcavePolygonShape3D`, which when dealing with complex collision meshes (or many/large `Area3D`) can end up being a lot. These contacts can add a lot of overhead both in terms of CPU and memory during the simulation step in ways that might not be easy to correlate to the source of the problem.\r\n\r\nThis new way of doing it is essentially exploiting the fact that `Area3D` in Godot doesn't actually expose the exact contacts between itself and the thing it's overlapping. This means that the underlying collision detection during simulation really only needs exactly one contact per shape, and that contact can be anywhere, which means we can set Jolt's underlying collision collector to be the much cheaper `JPH::AnyHitCollisionCollector` for any collision involving sensors/areas.\r\n\r\nI still need to do some profiling to see the exact gains (and potential losses) from this, but this should hopefully be relatively safe merge, apart from the breaking change.\r\n\r\nNote however that since we're now forced to always allow interactions between the broadphase layers belonging to areas and static bodies, this will presumably add some amount of additional cost to `Area3D`'s collision detection, for anyone who wasn't previously relying on this project setting, but it is what it is. Being diligent about using collision masks and layers properly (which should be done anyway) should hopefully mitigate some of that.\r\n\r\nCC: @jrouwe","labels":[{"id":73330066,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw3MzMzMDA2Ng==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/enhancement","name":"enhancement","description":"","color":"aaccff","default":true,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":370471880,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwzNzA0NzE4ODA=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:physics","name":"topic:physics","description":"","color":"ffee88","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":955079684,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw5NTUwNzk2ODQ=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/breaks%20compat","name":"breaks compat","description":"","color":"b64245","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":2666708289,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNjY2NzA4Mjg5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:3d","name":"topic:3d","description":"","color":"ffee88","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":3240950060,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwzMjQwOTUwMDYw","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/performance","name":"performance","description":"","color":"447777","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"milestone":{"id":12070367,"node_id":"MI_kwDOAO6SJc4AuC3f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/milestones/22","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/milestone/22","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/milestones/22/labels","number":22,"state":"closed","title":"4.5","description":"","creator":{"login":"Sauermann","id":6299227,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYyOTkyMjc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6299227?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sauermann","html_url":"https://github.com/Sauermann","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sauermann/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sauermann/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sauermann/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sauermann/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sauermann/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sauermann/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sauermann/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sauermann/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sauermann/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"open_issues":3,"closed_issues":3687,"created_at":"2024-12-19T08:51:28Z","updated_at":"2026-09-04T21:48:38Z","closed_at":"2025-09-18T17:13:14Z","due_on":"2025-09-15T00:00:00Z"},"active_lock_reason":null,"created_at":"2025-04-25T11:57:38Z","updated_at":"2025-06-05T11:25:40Z","closed_at":"2025-06-05T11:19:19Z","merged_at":"2025-06-05T11:19:19Z","merge_